  "cli_result_text": "Submitted. Summary of the root-cause chain found across both repos:\n\n**Babel side** (`packages/babel-plugin-proposal-decorators/src/index.ts`) branches on `legacy: true` \u2192 `transformer-legacy.ts`, a fork of `babel-plugin-transform-decorators-legacy`. That file builds `__decorate`-style calls but **never inspects TS type annotations or emits `design:type`/`design:paramtypes`/`Reflect.metadata` calls at all** \u2014 confirmed by reading `babel-plugin-transform-typescript/src/index.ts`, which only strips types (enums, namespaces, parameter properties) and has zero metadata-emission logic. Babel's stock toolchain (`preset-typescript` \u2192 `plugin-proposal-decorators`) structurally cannot produce NestJS's DI metadata; that behavior only exists via third-party packages like `babel-plugin-transform-typescript-metadata` (not in this repo), which the customer's babel pipeline evidently lacked.\n\n**SWC side**, `crates/swc_ecma_transforms_proposal/src/decorators/mod.rs` routes `legacyDecorator: true` to `legacy/mod.rs` (`TscDecorator`), which \u2014 only `if self.metadata` (wired from `.swcrc`'s `decoratorMetadata`) \u2014 runs `ParamMetadata` and `Metadata` visitors (`legacy/metadata.rs`) that read live `TsTypeAnn` nodes off class props/params/methods to synthesize `_ts_metadata(\"design:type\", ...)` calls, faithfully porting `tsc`'s `emitDecoratorMetadata`. Critically, `crates/swc/src/lib.rs` documents the pass-ordering guarantee: decorators are handled **before** `typescript::strip` runs, so type annotations are still present when `Metadata` visits the class \u2014 this is why SWC's legacy-decorator + decoratorMetadata combo works at all.\n\n**The divergence**: SWC requires *both* `jsc.transform.legacyDecorator: true` **and** `decoratorMetadata: true` (`crates/swc/src/config/mod.rs`, `bindings/binding_core_wasm/src/types.rs`) to emit the `_ts_metadata` calls Nest's `Reflect.getMetadata` reads at bootstrap. If the customer's `.swcrc` set `legacyDecorator: true` but left `decoratorMetadata` at its default `false`, SWC silently produces zero metadata \u2014 classes construct fine, decorators fire, but no `design:paramtypes` ever reaches `Reflect`, exactly matching the reported symptom. This is the config gap to check first, since it reproduces the bug without any Babel/SWC semantic bug at all.",
